{"availability":"available","full":"gabosarmiento/demotape","name":"demotape","description":"Make product demos agentically on macOS — your coding agent reads the codebase, scripts the scenes, drives the app, records, narrates, and verifies each scene before handing back the video. Or record yourself (screen or webcam) and let it auto-edit, caption, and voice over. Local-first, free & open source.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Swift","stars":14,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-08T02:21:10Z","updated":"2026-09-22T21:11:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["avfoundation","core-image","demo","intel-mac","macos","menubar","product-demo","screen-recorder","screen-recording","screencast","swift","video"],"demo":"https://kiff.dev/videos","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T18:44:10.557Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T18:44:10.557Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T18:44:10.557Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T18:44:10.557Z","stars":14,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Make a great demo of your app — fast, with your coding agent.","Describe the feature; your agent (Kiro, Claude Code, Codex…) reads the code, runs the app, records the flow, narrates it, and polishes — captions, voiceover, another language, a vertical cut. Or record it yourself and let DemoTape do the styling. Local-first, no account, free and open source.","Runs on macOS 12.3+ (Intel or Apple Silicon) — including older Macs like Monterey 12.7.6."],"features":["Product & feature demos — the agent drives your app and narrates what it's doing.","Launch clips & social cuts — vertical (9:16), square (1:1), captioned for muted autoplay.","Talking-head / webcam videos — a built-in teleprompter that never appears in the recording","Localized versions — re-voice the same footage in another language, no re-recording.","Proof that a change actually works — a verified demo of a pull request, with a per-scene"],"sourceU